Construction works on this stretch were very slow and the first fragment, from Września to [[Sługocin, Greater Poland Voivodeship|Sługocin]] ({{convert|34|km|mi}}) was opened in 1985. Until 1989 the motorway has been extended to Konin (additional {{convert|14|km|mi}}). At present, it is part of motorway A2.

As this fragment of highway was constructed during the [[Cold War]], the military function of mighty strip of solid ground was not forgotten. About {{convert|2|km|mi}} east of Września, both carriageways were designated only by [[Road surface marking|road markings]]{{R|zawistowski}} on {{convert|27|m|yd}}-wide piece of [[Asphalt concrete|asphalt]], which allowed to create a [[highway strip]], with length of {{convert|2.5|km|mi}}, that contained [[Airport apron|aprons]] on both ends. This specific road structure still exists, however appended with [[Traffic barrier|traffic barriers]] between carriageways and separating traffic from now-disused aprons.

