This part of ''Olimpijka'' was unfinished until 2010, however there were some viaducts, bridges and culverts, a [[Glade (geography)|glade]] in Bolimów Forest (with a forest road that had remnants of asphalt) and {{convert|700|m|yd}} of asphalt [[Unused highway|road to nowhere]]. One of the structures were rows of pillars that were supposed to carry a viaduct over then-proposed northern branch of Central Railway Line towards [[Gdańsk]] (which was never constructed). On some road maps the [[Bolimów]] – [[Wiskitki]] stretch was marked as ''highway in construction''. On almost entire length was an unpaved track, used by local population. Traces of earthworks and forestry work were visible on satellite imagery and aerial pictures to [[Stryków]].

In January 2010, as part of preparation to construction of motorway A2, [[deforestation]] was started, with additional works related to dismantling of then-existing viaducts.<ref>{{Citation |url = https://warszawa.wyborcza.pl/warszawa/7,34864,7431553,nie-do-wiary-zaczynaja-autostrade-do-stolicy.html |author = Krzysztof Śmietana |title = Nie do wiary: zaczynają autostradę do stolicy |trans-title = Unbelievable: they begin the motorway to the capital city |date = 8 January 2010 |access-date = 8 February 2022 |language = pl |magazine = [[Gazeta Wyborcza]]}}</ref> On 23 June 2010 the first of remnants was [[Demolition|destroyed]] – unfinished viaduct on the edge of Bolimów Forest, by blowing up. This fragment was opened to traffic in 2012.<ref>{{Citation |url = https://warszawa.wyborcza.pl/warszawa/7,54420,11877872,otworzyli-autostrade-a2-warszawa-polaczona-z-europa.html |author = Krzysztof Śmietana |title = Otworzyli autostradę A2! Warszawa połączona z Europą |trans-title = They have opened motorway A2! Warsaw connected with Europe |date = 6 June 2012 |access-date = 8 February 2022 |language = pl |magazine = Gazeta Wyborcza}}</ref>

On the night of 6–7 June 2012 the last section of constructed motorway has been opened near [[Wiskitki]]. It made possible to drive on former ''Olimpijka'' – 36 years after beginning of the first construction – from Warsaw through [[Poznań]] to [[Berlin]] and further without leaving the motorway.

